NEARS-2558 — AC4 regression-guard finding: LTR/1.0x settings-card top position is NOT
unchanged from pre-fix behavior on the QA pool device (emulator-5554, Pixel_10_Pro-class,
wm density 480 -> devicePixelRatio 3.0, wm size 1344x2992).

PRE-FIX (source, UserApp/lib/features/profile/screens/profile_screen.dart, diff 682c7521):
  - Positioned(
-            top: 180, left: 0, right: 0, bottom: 0,
    -> unconditional literal 180.0dp for the settings-card Positioned, on every device.

POST-FIX, measured LIVE via the Dart VM service debugDumpRenderTree
(http://127.0.0.1:59702/Z6cnDl0G9js=/ext.flutter.debugDumpRenderTree), locale=en (LTR),
adb shell settings get system font_scale => 1.0 (confirmed), package
com.izzes.nears.nears_nears_2558_guest_profile_login_cta, pid 28541:

  parentData: top=63.0; ...           <- 'profile'.tr title Positioned
  parentData: top=53.0; left=10.0 ... <- back-arrow Positioned (== MediaQuery.padding.top)
  parentData: top=108.0; ...          <- guest/logged-in header Row Positioned (padding.top + 55)
  parentData: top=206.0; right=0.0; bottom=0.0; left=0.0;   <- SETTINGS CARD Positioned (this fix's _settingsCardTop)

Cross-checked independently via uiautomator dump + `adb shell wm density` (480 -> 3.0 px/dp):
  settings-card container bounds (unlabeled android.view.View): [0,663][1344,2920] px
  663px / 3.0 = 221.0dp  (LTR/1.3x run) -- separately, the LTR/1.0x run's own uiautomator dump
  showed the card container at [0,618][1344,2920] px = 206.0dp, matching the render-tree
  value above exactly.

DELTA: 206.0dp (post-fix, LTR/1.0x) vs 180.0dp (pre-fix, all states) = +26.0dp / +78px shift,
on the explicit "should be unchanged" baseline case named by AC4.

ROOT CAUSE: MediaQuery.of(context).padding.top on this device is 53.0dp (from
`adb shell wm size`/`wm density` + the WindowInsets logcat line
"statusBars:[0,159,0,0]" -> 159px / 3.0 = 53.0dp), well above the ~24-31dp a typical
phone's status bar carries. _measureHeaderAndUpdate()'s headerTop = padding.top + 55 = 108dp,
+ header row height (~74dp, avatar-bound) = headerBottom ~182dp, + Dimensions.paddingSizeLarge
(20dp) = ~202-206dp > the 180dp floor -- so on THIS device the `math.max(180, measured)` floor
never actually activates even in the plain LTR/1.0x case, contradicting the fix's own inline
comment ("180 stays the floor so LTR/1.0x ... is unchanged by construction").

VISUAL IMPACT: benign in isolation -- docs/qa-evidence/NEARS-2558/ac4-ltr-1.0x-guest-profile.png
shows a clean, non-overlapping render (arguably nicer breathing room than the old fixed 180
would have given, which by the same math would have UNDERLAPPED the header content by ~2px
on this exact device -- i.e. pre-fix likely already had a tiny latent overlap here, unrelated
to RTL). But the literal AC4 text ("settings card position unchanged from current behavior")
is not satisfied: the position measurably changed.
